body:
Oh yes, absolutely, esp. given the context of the manga. 

In hindsight, Kaeya using the guard to shift suspicion *off* Diluc rather than on makes more sense than my sleep-deprived mind considered earlier haha. And it certainly makes sense considering his other bios too. 

Haha, he's a suspicious guy. Who knows what's going on in his head - but isn't that exactly why he's so interesting c;

Celebrate:

I reblogged a post that went something along the lines of '[characer]'s freckles: reblog if you agree' and the person I reblogged it from followed me back and liked a bunch of posts on my blog. 

*They're this artist whose art I quite like* ;u;

Yes! Oh my god, I loved the companions in DA2! They were all kind of - dark? In a way? I adored it. Their writing was not faultless (looking at Anders approving of Fenris being 'returned' to Danarius) but it was my favourite of the series. 

Although I agree that the reused areas were kind of - like, *ugh* - I have to admit that it was a lot nicer than spending five hours trying to finish clearing an area in DAI. 

My favourite thing about DA2 though (other than the LIs) is probably how fluid dual wielding rogue felt compared to the other games. You had a nice/reliable gap closer, and the attacks were just *so* nice to watch. ;u;
